# Summary
One or two sentences describing who you are, your current role, and your main stack. This is used
verbatim (or lightly quoted) to answer open-ended "tell us about yourself" fields Simplify leaves
blank — write it the way you'd actually want a recruiter to read it.

# Skills
- List every skill, language, framework, and tool you'd want an application to mention.
- One per line is fine — grouping into categories (Languages, Backend, DevOps, etc.) like below
  is optional but makes it easier for you to scan later.

# Experience
## Job Title, Company (Month Year – Month Year or "Present")
- What you actually did, one bullet per line.
- Be concrete — these get quoted directly into free-text answers, so only put things here you can
  stand behind in an interview.

## Previous Job Title, Previous Company (Month Year – Month Year)
- ...

# Education
- Degree, Field — Institution (Year – Year)

# Languages
- Language — Fluency level
